Fix command injection in RotateLogs (CWE-78)

The rotate verb passed the log name from the request into a /bin/sh -c command
string, so a name containing shell metacharacters ran arbitrary commands as
the service user. RotateLogs now rotates the one server log in place with
File.Move and takes no argument: there is no command string and no shell, so
no request input reaches a command interpreter.
